Description: ffmpeg: accept Plex's -strict_ts:N <int> as a no-op stub
 Plex's transcoder fork registers a top-level CLI option
 `-strict_ts <0|1>` (per-stream, help text "require strictly-
 increasing timestamps") in fftools/ffmpeg_opt.c — verified by
 grepping the literal symbol + help string out of `Plex
 Transcoder.real` 1.12.3 (jellyfin-ffmpeg's tree has no equivalent).
 PMS emits it on every subtitle-copy output (`-codec:N copy ...
 -strict_ts:N 0 -f srt`) — 130 hits across our 209-entry argv
 corpus — always with value `0` (lenient, the muxer default).
 .
 Stock jellyfin-ffmpeg's option parser doesn't know it and exits
 with "Unrecognized option strict_ts". The worker rewriter has
 historically stripped the flag (`drop:-strict_ts`, plus a copy in
 the bail path for side-channel SRT/audio sidecar argvs) to avoid
 the bail. The strip works because PMS's value `0` matches stock
 ffmpeg's default lenient subtitle-PTS handling — but the strip
 logic is rewriter bandaid B7 in `project_scaleplex_bandaid_retirement`.
 .
 This patch lands the same one-line OPT_TYPE_STRING sink pattern
 that 0098 used for `-loglevel_plex`: register the option, accept
 the value, discard it. The `:N` stream specifier is silently
 dropped by the option parser (find_option matches up to `:`,
 write_option without OPT_FLAG_SPEC ignores the suffix). Multiple
 occurrences just overwrite the global sink; we never read it.
 .
 Net effect: the rewriter can stop translating `-strict_ts*` for
 both the full-rewrite and bail paths, and PMS's argv passes
 through unchanged. Runtime behaviour identical to today's strip.
Origin: backport (minimal), scaleplex
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
---
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg.h
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg.h
@@ -731,6 +731,7 @@
 extern char *canthrottle_url;
 extern _Atomic int scaleplex_throttle_delay_us;
 extern char *plex_loglevel_sink;
+extern char *plex_strict_ts_sink;
 extern float max_error_rate;
 
 extern char *filter_nbthreads;
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg.c
@@ -105,6 +105,8 @@
 _Atomic int scaleplex_throttle_delay_us = 0;
 // scaleplex/PLEX: stub sink for `-loglevel_plex` (Plex CLI compat).
 char *plex_loglevel_sink = NULL;
+// scaleplex/PLEX: stub sink for `-strict_ts:N` (Plex CLI compat).
+char *plex_strict_ts_sink = NULL;
 
 InputFile   **input_files   = NULL;
 int        nb_input_files   = 0;
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg_opt.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg_opt.c
@@ -1581,6 +1581,13 @@
     // scaleplex/PLEX: accept Plex's -loglevel_plex <name> as a stub.
     { "loglevel_plex",          OPT_TYPE_STRING, OPT_EXPERT, { &plex_loglevel_sink },
         "Plex-style secondary log level (no-op stub for CLI compat)", "level" },
+    // scaleplex/PLEX: accept Plex's `-strict_ts:N <0|1>` as a stub.
+    // Help text from Plex Transcoder.real binary: "require strictly-
+    // increasing timestamps". PMS only ever emits value 0 (lenient,
+    // matches stock subtitle-PTS default). `:N` specifier is silently
+    // dropped by the parser; the global sink is write-only.
+    { "strict_ts",              OPT_TYPE_STRING, OPT_EXPERT, { &plex_strict_ts_sink },
+        "Plex-style strict-timestamps toggle (no-op stub for CLI compat)", "n" },
     { "progress",               OPT_TYPE_FUNC, OPT_FUNC_ARG | OPT_EXPERT,
         { .func_arg = opt_progress },
       "write program-readable progress information", "url" },
